      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Trench 4 Excavation Report Summary\n\nThe excavation of Trench 4 revealed a complex stratigraphic sequence, characterized by distinct changes in soil color and composition. The top layer (Unit 2) yielded a concentration of pottery shards, suggesting a possible occupation site. A significant shift in soil color and the presence of charcoal and a bone tool in Unit 3 indicate a possible fire or butchering activity. The bottom layer (Unit 4) consists of compact clay and flint flakes, possibly indicative of a later, more intense occupation. Notably, the layers appear to have been disturbed by previous excavation or animal activity, potentially affecting the stratigraphic integrity of the site.",
